  "standard": "PC.TRIG.B.1",
  "difficulty": 3,
  "prompt": "In one town the longest day of the year has $16$ hours of daylight and the shortest has $8$ hours. Daylight through the year follows a sine wave. What is the AMPLITUDE, in hours?",
  "answerType": "numeric",
  "primaryAnswer": "4",
  "alternativeAnswers": [],
  "acceptanceMode": "normalized",
  "hint": "Amplitude is HALF the distance from the highest point to the lowest point.",
  "hints": [
    {
      "level": "nudge",
      "text": "Amplitude is HALF the distance from the highest point to the lowest point."
    },
    {
      "level": "nudge",
      "title": "🪜 Try a simpler one",
      "text": "Practise on an easier wave: it peaks at $10$ and dips to $2$. The gap is $8$, so the amplitude is $8 \\div 2 = 4$. Now use the same two steps on $16$ and $8$."
    },
    {
      "level": "guide",
      "text": "The gap is $16 - 8 = 8$ hours. Halve it."
    },
    {
      "level": "reveal",
      "text": "$8 \\div 2 = 4$ hours."
    }
  ],
  "explanation": [
    "Peak $= 16$ h, trough $= 8$ h.",
    "Amplitude is the half-gap: $(16 - 8) \\div 2 = 8 \\div 2 = 4$ hours.",
    "Check with the midline: the middle is $(16 + 8) \\div 2 = 12$ h, and $12 + 4 = 16$, $12 - 4 = 8$. ✓"
  ],
  "alternativeExplanations": [
    {
      "title": "Find the midline first",
      "steps": [
        "The midline is the average of the two extremes: (16 + 8) ÷ 2 = 12 hours.",
        "The amplitude is how far the peak sits above that midline: 16 − 12 = 4 hours."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Build the equation",
      "steps": [
        "Write daylight = a·sin(x) + k. Peak means k + a = 16; trough means k − a = 8.",
        "Subtract the second from the first: 2a = 8, so a = 4 hours."
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tags": [
    "amplitude",
    "word-problem"
  ],
